From fba19c1d743a39c502dcd31585f8050dd4d951f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:03:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: report controller velocity from the streamed grip
 poses

The tracking packet carries no controller velocity, and xrLocateSpace answered every XrSpaceVelocity with zeros, while xrLocateSpaces flagged those zeros valid. Apps throw with the hand velocity at release, so in Half-Life: Alyx every thrown object dropped straight down.

InputManager now keeps the recent tracked grip samples per hand and differences them on the client timestamps over about 40 ms. LocateSpace adds the lever arm to the space origin, expresses both vectors in the base space, and sets the valid bits only when it knows: a hand with two samples, or a fixed reference space, located in a fixed base. xrLocateSpaces passes on what LocateSpace gives.
---
